From f30a32f6717f1a4b152e82376dfa6cc9ba7235f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gunnm92 <gunnm44@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:18:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(linux): DualSense USB/IP backend via vhci-hcd

Add UsbipGamepad, selected for the USB DualSense profile when
LIBVIRTUALHID_DUALSENSE_USBIP=1. The emulated device is served by the
ds5usbip library (DualSenseDevice, UsbipSession) on one end of a
socketpair, and the other end is attached to vhci-hcd through its
attach file. On any failure the one-line reason goes to stderr and the
existing uhid path is used.

Output reports are queued from the session threads and dispatched by a
worker thread, so the output callback never runs on a session thread.

Tests drive the vhci side of the socketpair from the fixture: attach
line, descriptors, SET_CONFIGURATION, input reports, a 200-report
output burst, the pairing feature report and close.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
